  "result": "I fixed it, and `Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py`, `Cart.remove` checked each line's item **name** instead of its **SKU** (`l.item.name != sku`). `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so the filter kept every line and nothing was removed. Removing by name `'Widget'` would have worked.\n\n**Fix:** changed the comparison to `l.item.sku != sku`, so it matches how `Cart.add` identifies lines.\n\n**Tests:** there wasn't a test for `Cart.remove`, so I added `test_remove_by_sku` to `tests/test_pricing.py`. It builds the same cart as the demo, removes `sku-1`, and checks that only `sku-2` is left. All 7 tests pass (run with `python3 -m unittest`, since there's no `python` on this machine). `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, the one Gadget left. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
